@startuml

title A publish request: the states of the approval that authorises a set

[*] --> Waiting : raise a publish\n(no stated rule closes it)
Waiting --> Held : hold
Held --> Waiting : resume
Waiting --> Approved : a person approves,\nor a stated rule\ncloses the request
Held --> Withdrawn : the asker takes it back
Waiting --> Withdrawn : the asker takes it back
Waiting --> Refused : a person refuses
Waiting --> Expired : the window passes\nwith nobody deciding
Approved --> [*] : the trader applies it,\nwhich publishes the set
Refused --> [*]
Expired --> [*]
Withdrawn --> [*]

Waiting : one open request\nper subject and as-of
Held : parked pending a question
Approved : waits on the trader,\nwho is not the decider
Refused : final; a new request\nis a new raise
Expired : final; the subject is\nfree for a new raise
Withdrawn : final; nothing\nwas published

note right of Approved
  The apply is a separate act and not a state
  of the request. A request publishes once;
  a second apply is refused, and the next
  publish is a new request.
end note

@enduml
